  "enforce_mode_error": "MIS_G7_DIRECT_PACKING_DENIED (42501): direct bulk-affecting event_skus INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE and header reassign/retype/delete are refused unless made by mis_pack_fg_bulk_v1 / mis_correct_pack_line_v1 in the same transaction.",
  "legacy_editor_note": "rpc_update_daily_work_log_with_packaging (30 arguments, DEFINER, module:edit-log-entry edit; sha256 4c82b4a3...d7b4) and fn_parse_sku_breakdown (sha256 ec5fe3ea...29db) are NOT changed. The __core (live sha256 df7290df...6aec) is changed only by migration S5b (one function-local plpgsql directive + three added statements; patched sha256 dfa5a5e9...1bcc), which is owner-gated; its client contract is unchanged (same arguments, same result columns daily_work_log_id/packaging_event_id/inserted_event_sku_count, same sku_breakdown grammar e.g. '40 g x 576; 10 mL x 480'). Under AUDIT everything behaves as today; ENFORCE additionally needs the owner sign-off for the patched SHA. New refusal exceptions raised by the editor in either mode when a bulk-affecting chain would violate the rules (whole edit rolled back): MIS_G7_CHAIN_STAGE_NOT_SIGNED, MIS_G7_CHAIN_STAGE_SOURCE_CHANGED, MIS_G7_CHAIN_CONSERVATION_MISMATCH, MIS_G7_CHAIN_BATCH_IDENTITY_MISSING, MIS_G7_CHAIN_SKU_INVALID, MIS_G7_CHAIN_EVENT_NOT_DEPLETING, MIS_G7_CHAIN_REPLACE_NOT_FINISHED (SQLSTATE P0001).",
  "s7_status": "PREPARED, NOT INSTALLED. The four S7 read RPCs below exist only after owner-authorized installation of 20261124120000 (S7a) and 20261124121000 (S7b). Clients must treat their absence (42883 / PGRST202) as \"S7 not installed\" and fall back to the S2\u2013S6 contract."
